{
  "_comment": [
    "Every hosted alias the example configs use, and the OpenRouter model it named when",
    "the committed runs were measured. One table for all six examples.",
    "",
    "Two ways to reach these models, chosen by `_shared/gateway.py` at call time:",
    "  * your own LiteLLM proxy -- LITELLM_BASE_URL + LITELLM_API_KEY; the proxy owns the",
    "    alias mapping (litellm.config.yaml in this directory is that mapping, ready to use);",
    "  * OpenRouter directly -- OPENROUTER_API_KEY alone; the mapping comes from here.",
    "",
    "Captured from the proxy's /model/info when the sweeps ran. NOT a version pin:",
    "OpenRouter can update or retire an upstream id, and a rerun records what served it.",
    "`self_test` checks this table against every config and every committed run."
  ],
